e for a  while it would make sense for him to go  east and then you know that would open a  lot of doors and in the way of him  finding something that could be of value  to her in her quest later my personal  hope is that he will run into Quaithe  but the show hasn't used her much and  she's a lot bigger of a character in the  books it would be cool since Quaithe is  a really interesting character it is  important but not exactly sure why he  would need to run into her face to face  if you don't remember Cuesta's the mask  shadow binder woman Dany met in Qarth  that actually approached Jorah first and  you know she gives Dany some help and  some profit  see that is pretty important in the  books Quaithe communicates with Danny  and dreams and there is a high  likelihood that she is secretly another  character from the past I always like  the shardene theory since I think ishara  has more of a role to play in the story  but other theories say she's shear a sea  star who is one of the great bastards  that's a sister to Bloodraven if he  doesn't run into Quaithe maybe he finds  out something about the warlocks from  the house of the undying there's a  possibility that since you're on Greyjoy  is getting into the mix that they might  be important but I am working on a your  own video that will get into that so I'm  not really going to talk about that here  let me know what you guys think about  where Jorah will end up and what he'll  do I mentioned in my last season 7th  video that we are getting confirmed  battle at sea that pits the Greyjoy's  against one another we also have news  that they are casting for other battles  which means a season looks like there's  going to be a whole lot of stuff going  on Watchers on the wall reported the  Game of Thrones is casting hundreds of  extras in Spain they have pretty strict  rules which include no visible tattoos  or modern hairstyles it's also been  mentioned that the male's must be  willing to shave their heads and beard  